# ~/.secrets/main.env — shared devbox credentials, auto-exported into EVERY shell
# (login + interactive) by /etc/profile.d/devbox-env.sh baked into the image.
# Lives at persisted ~/.local/secrets/main.env (0600, dir 0700). See docs/06.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# RULE: only LITERAL values (or vars no tool reads directly) belong here.
# An auto-exported variable SHADOWS CLI logins — e.g. a GITHUB_TOKEN line here
# overrides `gh auth login`'s stored credentials in every shell, and if that value
# is a vault reference like op://... instead of a real token, gh breaks with
# "token invalid". Vault references belong in per-project .env.op files.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# 1Password service account (read-only vault access) — this one IS safe here,
# because only the `op` CLI reads it, and it makes `op` work in every shell:
# OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN=ops_...

# Bitwarden alternative (see docs/06 — bw needs an unlock step per session):
# BW_CLIENTID=user.xxxxxxxx
# BW_CLIENTSECRET=...

# Cross-project literals (examples):
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
